course: dictionary
lesson: 5201
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word jam is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «We spread strawberry jam on our toast.» The clues are spread and toast, so jam is a sweet food made from fruit and sugar.
explain: «The bus sat in a traffic jam for an hour.» The clues are traffic, sat and for an hour. Many cars were stuck, so jam means cars that cannot move. Always test your meaning: put it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Jam can also be a verb, a doing word. «The sailor jammed his raft into the Whale's throat.» Jammed means pushed tightly into a space and got stuck there. Jam, jams, jammed and jamming are all the same word in different forms.
fact: «Jam» as a noun means a sweet food made from fruit and sugar, spread on bread.
fact: «Jam» as a noun can also mean a traffic jam: many cars stuck and not moving.
fact: «Jam» as a verb means to get stuck, or to push something tightly into a space.
fact: «In a jam» means in a difficult situation, and you may need help.
fact: If a machine or printer jams, ask an adult for help and turn it off.
exercise: «We spread strawberry jam on our toast.» What is jam here? | To play music together | Many cars stuck and not moving | A thin pancake | *A sweet food made from fruit and sugar
exercise: «The bus sat in a traffic jam for an hour.» What does jam mean here? | *Many cars stuck and not able to move | A sweet food made from fruit | To play music freely | A difficult situation with no way out
exercise: «The printer jammed, so Mum turned it off.» What does jammed mean? | Spread thickly on bread | Played loudly | Cooked with sugar | *Got stuck
test: «The sailor jammed his raft into the Whale's throat.» What does jammed mean here? | To sing a song with friends | To cook fruit with sugar | To spread something on bread | *To push something tightly into a space
test: Leo says, «We are in a jam.» What does he mean? | They have a new machine to fix | *They are in a difficult situation and need help | They are playing music together | They are eating jam on toast
exam: Ella reads, «The machine jammed, so we called an adult.» Which meaning fits best? | Sweet food made from fruit | Played music together | Many cars in a traffic queue | *Got stuck and stopped working
